<title>USA: Boise Cascade Office Q4 net flat, revs rise.</title>
<headline>Boise Cascade Office Q4 net flat, revs rise.</headline>
<dateline>ITASCA, Ill. 1997-01-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>BOISE CASCADE OFFICE PRODUCTS CORP</p>
<p>THREE MONTHS ENDED DECEMBER 31	   1996		  1995</p>
<p> Net sales				 $ 556,680	  $ 374,911</p>
<p> Gross profit				144,460	    100,120</p>
<p> Net income				   14,472	     14,761</p>
<p> EPS						 .23		  .24</p>
<p> Actual average shrs outstanding  62,658,813	 62,286,202</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>YEAR ENDED DECEMBER 31			  1996	    1995</p>
<p> Net sales				  $ 1,985,564   $ 1,315,953</p>
<p> Cost of sales				1,467,368	 980,564</p>
<p> Gross profit				   518,196	 335,389</p>
<p> Net income					55,349	  43,179</p>
<p>EPS and pro forma EPS</p>
<p>(based on 62,444,170 actual average</p>
<p>shares outstanding for the year ended</p>
<p>December 31, 1996, vs 61,660,100 pro</p>
<p>  forma average shares outstanding	    .89	     .70</p>
<p>		 (In thousands, except share data)</p>
<p>NOTE: Results are restated to reflect a two-for-one stock split.</p>
<p>On April 13, 1995, Boise Cascade Office completed an IPO of 10.6 million shares at $12.50 each. After the IPO, Boise Cascade Corp owned 82.7 percent of Boise Cascade Office Products.</p>
<p>EPS for the 1996 quarter, 1996 year and 1995 quarter are based on average shares outstanding, including common shares issued to effect acquisitions and shares issued as a result of stock options exercised.</p>
<p>1995 year EPS are presented assuming the 50.75 million common shares issued to Boise Cascade Corp in the organization of the company and the 10.6 million shares issued in the IPO were issued on January 1, 1995.</p>
